    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0584" n="1318" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1318"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-10-02"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October 2, 1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Monday several hundred Armenians marched on the Porte professedly to ask redress
                    of grievances. The patriarch tried to prevent it. A conflict occurred between
                    Armenians and police. Probably about 60 Turks and Armenians killed—among others
                    Turkish major—and many wounded. Armenians carried pistols. Yesterday several
                    more were killed. Last night 80 killed. Several hundred imprisoned. Porte had
                    notice of the demonstration, which they say was organized by leaders of
                    Huntchaguist revolutionists, whom they have captured. Much terror exists. I
                    think Porte will be able to restrain fanaticism.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
